## 🔍 Overview

This tutorial series focuses on the primary concepts of C#, starting with foundational console (terminal) applications and expanding into robust software design paradigms, data structures, and .NET features.

---

## 📖 Course Structure & Topics

### 1. Fundamental Concepts & Introductory Console Applications
* Introduction to Microsoft Visual Studio
* Values, Variables, Operators, and Operands
* Logical Operations, Equalities, Conditional Statements, Conjunctions, and Disjunctions
* Functions, Parameters, and Arguments
* Values vs. References
* Introduction to Classes, Namespaces, Methods, and Properties
* Constructors, Object Construction, and Destruction
* Tuples, Enumerations, and Conditional Switches

### 2. Objects and Object-Oriented Programming
* Class Inheritance and Value/Object Staticity
* Libraries and .NET Built-In Classes
* Nullity, Nullity Operators, and Exception Handling
* Inheritance using the `base` class
* Polymorphism, Abstraction, and Sealing Classes
* Interfaces, Built-In Interfaces, and Pattern Matching

### 3. Intermediate Topics & Building Objects
* Structures and Value Types Characteristics
* Bit Manipulations
* Console Data Reading and Writing
* Records, Arrays, Counting, and Looping
* Multidimensional Arrays (Primitive Types, Classes, Records, and Structures)

### 4. Advanced Concepts & Operations
* The Array Class and Common Array Operations
* Characters, Strings, and Text Processing Operations
* Generics and Inheritance
* Attributes
* Delegates and .NET Delegates
* Indexers and Classes
* Errors, Debugging, and Separate Files
* Operator Overloading

